ight heparin (LMWH) anticoagulant.","mechanism":"LMWH potentiates antithrombin, predominantly reducing factor Xa activity.","use":"Prevention or treatment of venous thromboembolism and anticoagulation in selected ACS regimens. Follow the indication-specific order and protocol. Some STEMI regimens include an ordered initial IV bolus.","administration":"For a prescribed SC dose, give deep SC at alternating abdominal sites. For a full dose from a manufacturer prefilled syringe, follow the product instructions, including leaving the air bubble in place and avoiding rubbing afterward. Never give IM.","monitor":"• Verify syringe strength and the ordered dose. Assess for bleeding and check platelets and renal function as ordered. • Severe renal impairment (CrCl below 30 mL/min) requires regimen review because enoxaparin exposure increases. • Report the dose and time of the last injection before an invasive procedure or neuraxial catheter placement/removal. • New midline back pain, leg weakness or numbness, or bowel/bladder dysfunction after a neuraxial procedure requires immediate escalation for possible spinal hematoma.","why":"Bleeding risk, renal clearance and timing make the exact syringe and dose important.","availability":"YES. Palestinian essential-medicine data document prefilled 20-, 40-, 60- and 80-mg syringes. ED shelf/drawer label photographed, 2 Nov 2026. This is a named compartment, not an independently audited stock count; check the package before use."},"readingSections":[{"field":"drugclass","label":"Drug class","text":"Low-molecular-weight heparin (LMWH) anticoagulant.","id":"section-0-5bd6cd7f5b5a6c33"},{"field":"mechanism","label":"Mechanism of action","text":"LMWH potentiates antithrombin, predominantly reducing factor Xa activity.","id":"section-1-dd342ba808e70aee"},{"field":"use","label":"Main use","text":"Prevention or treatment of venous thromboembolism and anticoagulation in selected ACS regimens. Follow the indication-specific order and protocol.