ivity."}],"point":"Identify the principal pharmacological action taught for this medicine.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ccu-norepinephrine--comprehensive--principal-action","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ccu-norepinephrine::principal-action"],"answerKey":"C"},{"format":"single-best-answer","stem":"Which drug class does NOREPINEPHRINE / NORADRENALINE belong to?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Catecholamine","explanation":"The medicine is classified as: Catecholamine vasopressor; predominantly alpha1 with beta1 activity."},{"id":"B","text":"Organic nitrate","explanation":"The medicine is classified as: Catecholamine vasopressor; predominantly alpha1 with beta1 activity."},{"id":"C","text":"Inotrope","explanation":"The medicine is classified as: Catecholamine vasopressor; predominantly alpha1 with beta1 activity."},{"id":"D","text":"Vasopressor","explanation":"Catecholamine vasopressor; predominantly alpha1 with beta1 activity."}],"point":"Identify the drug class taught for this medicine.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ccu-norepinephrine--comprehensive--drug-class","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ccu-norepinephrine::drug-class"],"answerKey":"D"},{"format":"single-best-answer","stem":"An adult in septic shock remains hypotensive after initial fluid resuscitation. There is no evidence of concomitant cardiac dysfunction. Which infusion is the usual first-line vasopressor?","choices":[{"text":"Norepinephrine","explanation":"Norepinephrine is the usual first-line vasopressor in this setting.","id":"A"},{"text":"Epinephrine","explanation":"Epinephrine can be used in selected situations, such as inadequate MAP despite initial vasopressors.","id":"B"},{"text":"Vasopressin","explanation":"Vasopressin is typically added as norepinephrine requirements rise.","id":"C"},{"text":"Dopamine","explanation":"Dopamine has selected uses but is not the usual first-line vasopressor in adult septic shock.","id":"D"}],"point":"Norepinephrine is the usual first-line vasopressor in adult s