antly beta1 inotrope."},{"id":"D","text":"Vasopressor","explanation":"The medicine is classified as: Predominantly beta1 inotrope."}],"point":"Identify the drug class taught for this medicine.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ccu-dobutamine--comprehensive--drug-class","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ccu-dobutamine::drug-class"],"answerKey":"C"},{"format":"single-best-answer","stem":"An adult in septic shock has adequate volume status and target MAP on norepinephrine. The team finds reduced cardiac contractility and ongoing hypoperfusion. Which change adds inotropic support while maintaining the current vasopressor?","choices":[{"text":"Replace norepinephrine with dobutamine.","explanation":"Removing current vasopressor support may jeopardize MAP.","id":"A"},{"text":"Add vasopressin while continuing norepinephrine.","explanation":"Vasopressin adds vasopressor effect and does not directly provide the inotropic support requested.","id":"B"},{"text":"Add dobutamine while continuing norepinephrine.","explanation":"Dobutamine can support cardiac output while norepinephrine maintains arterial pressure.","id":"C"},{"text":"Increase norepinephrine and defer inotropic support.","explanation":"MAP is already adequate. The unresolved problem is low output with hypoperfusion.","id":"D"}],"point":"Dobutamine can be added to norepinephrine for persistent hypoperfusion with cardiac dysfunction despite adequate fluids and BP.","criticalForSafety":true,"answerKey":"C","id":"ccu-dobutamine--comprehensive--treatment-role","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ccu-dobutamine::treatment-role"],"revision":"drug-dependent-20261106","sourceFields":["use"]},{"stem":"Which new change during DOBUTAMINE infusion is a relevant cardiac adverse-effect warning?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Improving alertness without rhythm change","explanation":"This does not identify the rhythm warning."},{"id":"B","text":"New tachycardia or ventricular ectopy","explanation":"Catecholamine effects can increase rhythm 