-role","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ccu-dobutamine::treatment-role"],"reusedFromQuestionId":"ccu-dobutamine--standard--treatment-role","answerKey":"D"},{"stem":"Which new change during DOBUTAMINE infusion is a relevant cardiac adverse-effect warning?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"New tachycardia or ventricular ectopy","explanation":"Catecholamine effects can increase rhythm instability."},{"id":"B","text":"Improving urine output without rhythm change","explanation":"This may support improved perfusion rather than identify arrhythmia."},{"id":"C","text":"Improving peripheral warmth without rhythm change","explanation":"This can reflect a beneficial perfusion response."},{"id":"D","text":"Improving alertness without rhythm change","explanation":"This does not identify the rhythm warning."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"Vasoactive stimulation can provoke tachycardia or ectopy.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ccu-dobutamine--7-day--tachyarrhythmia","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ccu-dobutamine::tachyarrhythmia"],"reusedFromQuestionId":"ccu-dobutamine--standard--tachyarrhythmia","answerKey":"A"},{"stem":"Which feature is required for safe IV administration of DOBUTAMINE?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Undiluted rapid injection based on the ampoule’s full volume","explanation":"Container content is not a default patient bolus."},{"id":"B","text":"Controlled infusion using the product-specific preparation and order","explanation":"Delivery and concentration must follow the authorized infusion regimen."},{"id":"C","text":"Intermittent manual boluses using the last infusion’s mL/hour","explanation":"An infusion rate cannot define a safe bolus."},{"id":"D","text":"Gravity flow without accounting for the prepared concentration","explanation":"Accurate controlled dosing depends on the concentration and delivery device."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"Use controlled, product-appropriate IV infusion rather than an improvised rapid bolus.","criticalForSafet